  "title": "# Amber chat: one UI asset + rename Gizmo -> Amber (Brett, Nov 7) Rule: every UI element is an asse…",
  "asked": "# Amber chat: one UI asset + rename Gizmo -> Amber (Brett, Nov 7) Rule: every UI element is an asset. The AmberX companion chat (apps/amberx-droid/src/plugins/companion/web: Chat.tsx, index.tsx, companion.css) is a plain component. Styling already uses tokens (no hard-coded values) — keep it that way. ## 1. Chat as an asset (Fable: contract) - Define/extend the shared chat UI asset type (reuse an existing chat/build-chat@1/assistant asset type if one fits; else a new `chat-view@1` in framework/assets with schema, both validators, fixture, check). Covers layout, message bubbles, input bar, voice/talk controls, header, empty/no-provider states. - Chat.tsx renders from the asset. The console AI assistant chat should be able to use the same asset (same assistant@1 plugin backs both). ## 2. Rename Gizmo -> Amber, safely - Inventory every `gizmo` reference first (code, ids, settings keys, storage paths, docs, persona, voice). Save the list in the report. - Rename to Amber everywhere: ids, files, labels, persona, voice. - Migrate saved chats/settings to new keys; dry-run the migration on a copy first and verify it loads. - Keep `gizmo` as an alias that resolves to Amber (old links/settings/commands keep working). - Back up old data; one-step rollback. - CI check: fails if `gizmo` appears anywhere except the alias table and migration. ## 3. UI Review with choices - Submit THREE distinct looks for the Amber chat (phone + desktop shots) to UI Review with --choices, so Brett picks one in the Choices tab. The pick becomes the asset's default. ## 4. Tests + Shipped features All AmberX + console tests green; add to Shipped features. Progress: append `<time> START|DONE <step>` to PROGRESS.md here at each step; don't stop between steps. Commit, don't push. No hard-coded styling. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.",
